Z||000000||Racer 1||07-09-99||10:54 PM||||Hello you fiero nuts does you battery leak like a faucet on a hot day?Mine does and I need to info on how to stop it.My battery has the filler hole on top its not a self concelled battery should I get a concelled battery? HELP HELP HELP HELP my fingers hurt from the battery acid and eyes to 8-(
Z||000001||Lynx||07-10-99||02:49 AM||||I dont have that problem and havent heard of it. My bet is that it is the battery, when they go bad i have seen this happen. I would replace the battery and if you can afford it by a fully sealed one like a Optima but they cost like $110 to $150. If it leaks it will eat the battery basket and you will have to replace it too (not to fun). I have a simple wal-mart ever start and have no problems and it was 98 degree's here today. Just to let every one know ever start is actually a good battery. They are made by the same company as Die-hard. Go cheap and go to Wal-mart by the same battery with out a big name for WAY cheaper.
Z||000002||theogre||07-11-99||06:25 PM||||go to K/Wall-mart and buy a battery. That one has some sort of problem, and it's not worth screwing with it. make sure you clean up the mess you have, and hit it with some backing soda to kill the acid you've spilt.
Z||000003||theogre||07-11-99||11:21 PM||||I forget who makes wallmart/diehard batteries. I do know Exide makes K-Marts, and I've only had one Exide ever fail short of it's full life. Funny thing about that is I replaced it with the next class smaller, physically anyway, battery........... The exact battery my 87sc needed when I bought it. (The battery was in another car when it failed......... a car with room for a bigger one. I always use the biggest one that fit the hole, but then I used to live in NY with it's screwy winters. Extra battery juice was a must.)
Z||000004||Carrolles||07-12-99||11:23 AM||||Replacing the battery may be only treating the symptom and not addressing the cause of the problem.  It sounds like the battery is being overcharged.  I'd suggest having your charging system checked out.  WalMart, AutoZone, etc. will do this for free.<p>Good luck,<br>Carroll
Z||000005||Lynx||07-12-99||12:20 PM||||Orge, A company called Johnson Controls Battery Group, Inc. They used to not make Die hard another group did. A few years ago Die hard changed too Johnson (At least the guy at Sears said that).
Z||000006||PaUL||07-12-99||02:09 PM||||Ive got a battery I bought from Wallmart. I was looking at it the other day, it said made by AC Delco, Flint MI on the side in small print.
Z||000007||theogre||07-12-99||07:36 PM||||Checking the charging system is like some sort of reflex for me...... I always forget to tell people to do that. That battery is definatly fried tho.
Z||000008||Cooter||07-12-99||09:10 PM||||In the "for what its worth department": I have had poor luck with batteries made by GNB- they are sold through several different brand names-Champion was one of them. i have seven of them from different vehicles that have gone bad and if you didnt buy the extended warranty, after 12 months you were stuck with it. I will never buy another one because they would not honor their written warranty. They did exactly what was described in this thread- spill acid and require 20-30 amps to keep charged. 
Z||000009||mwbackus||07-12-99||11:31 PM||||Hmm.. this reminds me of the time that me and a friend were going to this party.  We were in his ol' ford maverick and pulled up to the place.  We got out and started to walk up to the door when we heard a loud boom.  After picking ourselves up from the ground we realized it came from his car.  Further inspection revealed that the battery had actually exploded.  It was not a pretty site, and the maverick ended up in the bone yard after a brief parts scavenge.
Z||000010||Carrolles||07-13-99||07:10 AM||||I used to buy Sears DieHard batteries with 6 year warranty.  They never seemed to last more than 3 years.  I was then stuck with having to take the pro-rated replacement from Sears which cost almost as much as a new battery.  And then the new battery would suffer the same way.<p>I started buying WalMart batteries about 6 years ago.  They are often on sale for a very good price and have all lasted from 3 to 4 years without fail.  When I need a replacement there is always a WalMart around.  No more high priced Sears batteries for me.<p>Take care,<br>Carroll
Z||000011||Dan||07-13-99||09:39 AM|||| Sounds like your battery has a shorted cell<br>which makes the regulator charge at high rates,therefore overcharging the good cells <br>and causing them to boil over. Boiling over is a sign of overcharging but it could also be in the regulator. Follow the good advice and have the charging system checked. 
